    "openapi": "3.0.0",
    "info": {
        "title": "API",
        "description": "## Sandbox environment\n\nThe sandbox (`https://api.sandbox.londonmedicallaboratory.com`) mirrors production but\nis **fully self-contained** \u2014 no real laboratory is involved. Every test registration is\n**resulted automatically**, with no manual lab or clinician step.\n\n### Automatic result lifecycle\n\nWhen you create a test registration in the sandbox (`POST /api/test_registration/`):\n\n1. It is created with `status: \"pending\"` and `results_ready: false`.\n2. A **mocked lab** returns results after a short delay (~30s). Values are grounded in\n   real historical data \u2014 realistic per-biomarker reference ranges, correct units, and\n   **sex-aware** where it matters (e.g. testosterone, ferritin) \u2014 and are **deterministic**\n   per (patient, product, scenario), so you can write reproducible assertions.\n3. A **simulated doctor sign-off** authenticates the results.\n4. The registration reaches `status: \"success\"`, `results_ready: true`, `completed_at`.\n   End to end this normally completes within **1\u20132 minutes**.\n\n### Forcing specific outcomes\n\nSet the `foreign_id` to `test:<scenario>[+<timing>][@<biomarkers>]:<your-ref>` to force a\nknown result (like Stripe test cards): e.g. `test:all_failed:ref-1`,\n`test:abnormal_high@LDL,CHO:ref-2`, `test:partial+instant:ref-3`. Scenarios include\n`success`, `abnormal_high`/`abnormal_low`, `all_failed`, `partial`, `one_failed`,\n`pending_forever`, `awaiting_auth`, `processing_error`. Call **`GET /api/sandbox/scenarios`**\nfor the full machine-readable catalogue. The resolved scenario is echoed back as\n`sandbox_scenario`.\n\n### Webhooks & error simulation\n\nPoint lifecycle webhooks at your own endpoint with **`PUT /api/webhook`** to receive the\nreal events (sample received, results complete, registration complete, ...). Force any\nHTTP error from any endpoint with `?force_status=<code>` (e.g. `401`, `429`, `500`).\n\n### Fetching results\n\nPoll the registration (`GET /api/test_registration/{id}` \u2014 watch `results_ready` /\n`status`) or the results (`GET /api/test_registration/{id}/lab_results`, which returns\n`204` until ready then `200`). Print the TRF and sample label with\n`GET /api/test_registration/{id}/trf` and `/label`.\n\n> These sandbox behaviours are **sandbox-only**. In production, registrations require\n> real laboratory processing and clinician authentication.\n",
        "version": "1.0.0"
    },
    "paths": {
        "/api/appointment/": {
            "get": {
                "tags": [
                    "Appointment"
                ],
                "operationId": "get_app_api_appointmentaction_appointment_listpaginated",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "start_date",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Only results created after this value",
                        "required": false,
                        "example": "2020-12-30"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "end_date",
                        "in": "query",
                        "description": "Only results created before this value",
                        "required": false,
                        "example": "2025-12-30"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "default": {
                        "description": ""
                    }
                }
            },
            "post": {
                "tags": [
                    "Appointment"
                ],
                "description": "Create new appointment. Pass 'override_availability': true to book outside published working hours or into an unavailable slot, the way location portal staff can. Outside published hours no slot exists, so pass 'starts_at' (and 'test_location_id' when booking at another of your locations) instead of 'slot_id'.",
                "operationId": "post_app_api_appointmentaction_appointment_create",
                "requestBody": {
                    "description": "Create new appointment",
                    "content": {
                        "application/json": {
                            "schema": {
                                "properties": {
                                    "patient_id": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "example": null,
                                        "nullable": true
                                    },
                                    "slot_id": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "example": "1234-5678",
                                        "nullable": true
                                    },
                                    "starts_at": {
                                        "description": "Used when no slot_id is given, and required when overriding availability outside published hours",
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "example": "2025-04-12T15:00:00+00:00",
                                        "nullable": true
                                    },
                                    "test_location_id": {
                                        "description": "Location to book at, when it is not the authenticated brand. Must belong to the same organization",
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "example": null,
                                        "nullable": true
                                    },
                                    "confirmed": {
                                        "type": "boolean",
                                        "example": true,
                                        "nullable": false
                                    },
                                    "override_availability": {
                                        "description": "Book into a slot the calendar reports as closed, blocked or already taken",
                                        "type": "boolean",
                                        "example": false,
                                        "nullable": true
                                    }
                                },
                                "type": "object"
                            }
                        }
                    }
                },
                "responses": {
                    "default": {
                        "description": ""
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/api/appointment/{id}": {
            "get": {
                "tags": [
                    "Appointment"
                ],
                "operationId": "get_app_api_appointmentaction_appointment_getone",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "id",
                        "in": "path",
                        "required": true,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "default": {
                        "description": ""
                    }
                }
            },
            "delete": {
                "tags": [
                    "Appointment"
                ],
                "description": "Cancel an appointment. The appointment is kept for the record with status 'cancelled', and its slot is released for someone else to book.",
                "operationId": "delete_app_api_appointmentaction_appointment_cancel",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "id",
                        "in": "path",
                        "required": true,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "The cancelled appointment"
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "The appointment is not in a state that can be cancelled"
                    }
                }
            },
            "patch": {
                "tags": [
                    "Appointment"
                ],
